Next.js 16 App Router requires dynamic route handlers to accept `params` as a Promise. Five route files under `src/app/api/**/[id]/route.ts` were using the old synchronous signature, breaking Vercel builds.

## Changes

Updated 13 route handlers across 5 files:
- `cases/[id]/route.ts` - GET, PATCH, DELETE
- `clients/[id]/route.ts` - GET, PATCH, DELETE  
- `sessions/[id]/route.ts` - GET, PATCH, DELETE
- `messages/[id]/route.ts` - GET, DELETE
- `invoices/[id]/route.ts` - PATCH, DELETE

## Implementation

Added type helper and updated signatures:

```typescript
type IdContext = { params: Promise<{ id: string }> };

// Before
export async function GET(
  _req: NextRequest,
  { params }: { params: { id: string } }
) {
  const { id } = params;
  // ...
}

// After
export async function GET(
  _req: NextRequest,
  context: IdContext
) {
  const { id } = await context.params;
  // ...
}
```

All routes already use `requireAuthedSupabase()` for authentication - no dev fallbacks to remove.

